==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|strac||straight}}, from {{inh|de|goh|strac}} (attested in {{m|goh|framstrac}}), from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*strakkaz||straight}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*streg-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*treg-||stiff, rigid}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|strak}}. More at {{m|en|stretch}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ʃtʁak/|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|ak|lang=de}}

===Adjective===
{{de-adj|stracker|stracksten}}

# {{lb|de|archaic|or|dialectal}} [[straight]], [[taut]]
# {{lb|de|colloquial}} [[drunk]]

====Usage notes====
* Now almost exclusively used in the figurative sense “drunk” and in the adverbial form {{m|de|stracks|t=directly}}.

